{"seq":1,"mint":"C3","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":false,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"The `Search` observation's label is the only part of a grep census that reaches a committed memo","clause_quoted":true,"facts":[],"why":"The grep census creates per-file GrepMatch observations with their own labels, and the Facts renderer emits labels from each fact's extent. Therefore a GrepMatch label can reach the committed memo; the Search label is not the only label that can do so.","quoted":false,"rejected_span":"        for (file, matches) in by_file {\n            let m = world.for_path(Path::new(&file));\n            buf.push(PendingEntry {\n                captured_at: workspace::now_unix(),\n                kind: ObservationKind::GrepMatch,\n                key: resolve_key(Path::new(&file)),\n                label: format!(\"{file} (grep: {pattern})\"),\n                output: matches.join(\"\\n\"),\n                world_root: m.root,\n                world_state: m.state,\n                pattern: pattern.to_string(),\n            });\n        }\n\n        let extent = f\n            .extent\n            .iter()\n            .map(|e| e.label.as_str())\n            .collect::<Vec<_>>()\n            .join(\"; \");\n        out.push_str(&format!(\n            \"| {} | {} | {} | {} |\\n\",\n            ledger_cell(&f.id),\n            ledger_cell(&f.note),\n            ledger_cell(&extent),"}],"at":1790113072,"cost":0.0064884,"elapsed_ms":36749,"attempts":2,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":0,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0}
